# L §6.1 Writes into members: "A scenario over a joint model (§6.4) may replace the members' rows too, named with their
# prefixes (replace a.pay[ola] = 0 PLN): a scenario changes nothing in its base, and each member's files stay as
# pinned." The joint model of L6_1_joint; sx replaces a.rate by 0.2 from 2026: in sx ana's tax[2026] is
# 120 000 * 0.2 = 24 000 PLN (x), in the joint model still 120 000 * 0.12 = 14 400 PLN (x0), and ana's own ask a.q
# is unchanged (L §6.1 "joining changes no member's answer"). (Writer 8: was REFCORE-NOT-YET, scenarios of a joint
# model.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "26a08dc22b514dc0b6eb7c1263103f06b216244b4ed980752bbc810412d05e45"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "a8bf3b260e60f625766da425a660f922557f525c28dcf8ed70567ec64d600ccc"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index jy = year 2025..2027

def income_sum[y in jy]: num PLN = a.income[y] + b.income at reader

ask j1: income_sum[y] for y in jy law 2026-12-31
ask j2: a.tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
ask j3: a.rate law 2026-12-31
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2025..2027
input income[y in yrs]: money PLN
input rate: num
def tax[y in yrs]: num PLN = income[y] * rate at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income[2025] = 100 000.00 PLN
  income[2026] = 120 000.00 PLN
  income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN
  rate = 0.12

ask q: tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input income: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income = 80 000.00 PLN

ask q: income law 2026-12-31
=== sx.tally
scenario sx over family
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

source t "plan"

version up
  cite t
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-10-15
  replace a.rate = 0.2

ask x: a.tax[2026] in sx law 2026-12-31
ask x0: a.tax[2026] in family law 2026-12-31
=== expect x x0 a.q
x: 24 000 PLN
  world: sx
  held: a.rate = 0.2 (up), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
x0: 14 400 PLN
  world: family
  held: a.rate = 0.12 (a.v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
a.q: 14 400 PLN
  held: rate = 0.12 (v), read for 2026-12-31
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-10-20
